===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[passage]] of a [[door]]; a door-shaped [[entrance]] into a house or a room.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1950|month=February|title=Rolling Stock for London Transport|journal=Railway Magazine|page=88|text=A re-arrangement of the seating in relation to '''doorway''' positions gives an even distribution of seated passengers, no change has been made in the number or size of the '''doorways'''.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} An [[opening]] or [[passage]] in general.
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XLIII|66|How fares it with the happy dead?<br>For here the man is more and more;<br>⁠But he forgets the days before<br>God shut the '''doorways''' of his head [i.e. the sutures of the skull].}}

